description:
We are recruiting an **Artificial Intelligence (AI) Engineer** to strengthen our team, with the possibility of working remotely or in a hybrid model.


What we are looking for:

* Bachelors or Masters degree in Computer Science, Systems Engineering, Mathematics, Statistics, or related field;
* 3\-5 years of experience in AI, machine learning, and generative AI development (NLP, content generation, personalization, automation, recommendation systems);
* Experience in designing, developing, and optimizing AI models and algorithms;
* Experience in MLOps, AIOps, and GenAIOps for model deployment in production environments;
* Experience in programming with Python, R;
* In\-depth knowledge of AI frameworks (TensorFlow, PyTorch, Scikit\-learn, GPT, BERT or Stable Diffusion);
* Experience in data manipulation and processing with tools such as Pandas, NumPy and SQL;
* Experience in the management and configuration of vector databases;
* Familiarity with software architectures and cloud deployment (AWS, GCP, or Azure);
* Knowledge of hyperscaler AI and ML services (Amazon SageMaker, Vertex AI, Azure Machine Learning);
* Experience with CI/CD pipelines and version control systems;
* Experience with container technologies such as Docker and container orchestration tools such as Kubernetes;
* Experience with different communications protocols such as REST API or MQTT.


What we have to offer:

* Flexibility in the work regime (hybrid or remotely);
* Opportunity for professional growth in a growing company;
* Collaborative and supportive work environment;
* Competitive benefits package.


If you identify with this profile, send us your updated CV to recrutamento@movilges.com


If you want to learn more about us:


Movilges IT Consulting has over 30 years of experience in the Spanish market, specializing in Logistics, Mobility, and IT. We offer consulting services, application development, and system maintenance. Just as the technological universe is constantly evolving, Movilges IT Consulting aims to evolve as well, increasing its presence in Portugal. We strive not only to provide the best services to partners and clients but also to offer the best conditions, benefits, and professional growth opportunities for our entire team.


In Portugal, we are present in different sectors such as technology, health, public administration, energy, services, banking, and insurance.


By submitting your application, you authorize Movilges IT Consulting to process your personal data, such as name, email, phone number, and information about your academic and professional experiences as stated in your CV. The processing of this data serves only the legitimate purposes of the company, i.e., for the recruitment processes of qualified professionals for our team. For any questions related to your personal data, you can contact us at portugal@movilges.com

AgileEngine is an Inc. 5000 company that creates award\-winning software for Fortune 500 brands and trailblazing startups across 17\+ industries. We rank among the leaders in areas like application development and AI/ML, and our people\-first culture has earned us multiple Best Place to Work awards.




**WHY JOIN US**
 If you're looking for a place to grow, make an impact, and work with people who care, we'd love to meet you!




**ABOUT THE ROLE**
 We're looking for an experienced
 **Senior AI Engineer** 
 to join our elite consulting team. You'll work on diverse internal R\&D initiatives and high\-stakes client projects, delivering production\-ready AI systems that solve real business problems. This role combines deep technical expertise with client\-facing responsibilities. You'll architect solutions, lead implementation, and present to C\-level executives and technical stakeholders.




**WHAT YOU WILL DO**
 \- Design and implement end\-to\-end AI solutions for clients across various industries and use cases;


 \- Build sophisticated LLM applications using RAG, vector databases, fine\-tuning, and agentic workflows;


 \- Develop custom ML models for client\-specific challenges including NLP, computer vision, and predictive analytics;


 \- Independently assess, clean, and engineer features from complex, messy datasets;


 \- Own the complete data pipeline from ingestion through model training and deployment;


 \- Lead technical discovery sessions and solution architecture discussions with client stakeholders;


 \- Present technical concepts and project outcomes to executive leadership and technical teams;


 \- Mentor junior engineers and establish AI/ML best practices across client engagements;


 \- Collaborate with cross\-functional teams including product managers, designers, and business stakeholders;


 \- Contribute to internal R\&D initiatives and thought leadership in AI/ML.




**MUST HAVES**
 \-

 5\+ years of professional software development experience with strong fundamentals;


 \- 5\+ years deploying production machine learning systems at scale;


 \- 3\+ years of hands\-on experience with LLMs, including API integration and local deployment;


 \-
 **Strong data engineering and data science expertise—you can work with raw, unstructured data and transform it into ML\-ready datasets;**
**\- Proficiency with data manipulation tools: pandas, NumPy, SQL, and big data frameworks (Spark, Dask);**
 \- Expert\-level Python proficiency with deep knowledge of ML frameworks (PyTorch, TensorFlow, Hugging Face);


 \- Proven experience with modern AI techniques: RAG, vector search, prompt engineering, and agentic systems;


 \- Strong cloud platform expertise (AWS, GCP, Azure) with containerization and orchestration experience;


 \- Experience building scalable microservices, APIs, and ML inference pipelines;


 \-
 **Demonstrated ability to work independently and manage complex projects end\-to\-end with minimal oversight;**
 \- Exceptional communication skills with experience presenting to senior leadership;


 \- Consulting mindset with ability to understand business requirements and translate them into technical solutions;


 \- Track record of leading technical projects from conception to production deployment;


 \- Upper\-Intermediate English level.




**NICE TO HAVES**
 \- Previous consulting or client\-facing engineering experience;


 \- Experience across multiple industries (fintech, healthcare, e\-commerce, etc.);


 \-
 **Advanced statistical analysis and experimentation design experience;**
**\- Experience with streaming data platforms and real\-time ML systems;**
 \- Contributions to open\-source AI/ML projects or technical publications;


 \- Experience with MLOps, model monitoring, and deployment automation;


 \- Background in data engineering and large\-scale data processing;


 \- Advanced degrees in Computer Science, AI/ML, or related technical fields;


 \- Startup or fast\-paced environment experience.




**PERKS AND BENEFITS**
 \-
 **Professional growth:** 
 Accelerate your professional journey with mentorship, TechTalks, and personalized growth roadmaps.




 \-
 **Competitive compensation:** 
 We match your ever\-growing skills, talent, and contributions with competitive USD\-based compensation and budgets for education, fitness, and team activities.




 \-
 **A selection of exciting projects:** 
 Join projects with modern solutions development and top\-tier clients that include Fortune 500 enterprises and leading product brands.




 \-
 **Flextime:** 
 Tailor your schedule for an optimal work\-life balance, by having the options of working from home and going to the office – whatever makes you the happiest and most productive.

